### Topic 61 - API Gateway
### Start: eureka-server (8761) -> product-service (8081) -> order-service (8082) -> api-gateway (8080)
### From now on the client only talks to port 8080!

### 1. Route "product-route": /api/products/** -> lb://product-service
###    Look at the response headers: X-Powered-By and X-Correlation-Id were added by the gateway
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products

### 2. One product through the gateway
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products/1

### 3. Which headers did the service receive through the gateway?
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products/headers

### 4. Same endpoint DIRECTLY (bypassing the gateway) - no gateway headers
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products/headers

### 5. Route "shop-products-rewrite": /shop/products/2 is rewritten to /api/products/2
GET http://localhost:8080/shop/products/2

### 6. Discovery locator: automatic route /<service-id>/** for every Eureka service
GET http://localhost:8080/product-service/api/products/3

### 7. Place an order WITHOUT the API key -> 401 Unauthorized (blocked by ApiKeyGlobalFilter)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 2
}

### 8. Place an order WITH the API key -> 201 Created
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-KEY: course-secret-123

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 2
}

### 9. List orders through the gateway (GET does not need the key)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders

### 10. No route matches -> 404 from the gateway itself
GET http://localhost:8080/does-not-exist

### 11. Gateway actuator: every route the gateway knows
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/gateway/routes

### 12. External route (needs internet): /demo/get -> https://httpbin.org/get
GET http://localhost:8080/demo/get
